      "message": "DSP0267 Table 8 – Descriptor Identifier Table\n\ndefines `0x0002 - UUID`  as a valid initial descriptor for FrimwareDeviceIdentificationArea.\n\nSee the section about vendor defined descriptor\n```\nIf the Device or package header uses a Vendor\nDefined value then the initial descriptor shall be set\nto either PCI Vendor ID, IANA Enterprise ID, IEEE\nAssigned Company ID, or SCSI Vendor ID\n```\n\nso the initial descriptor is restricted further if there is a vendor defined descriptor present but for the device here there is only one descriptor which is not vendor defined. The device defined above this one has a vendor defined descriptor but it\u0027s different device.\n\nIn my interpretation it means that it is fine.\n\nLet me know if there is some other interpretation which you think is more appropriate.",
